 "structure": "Single PDF 'Academic Standards for History' (Final Form Annex A, July 18 2002; 22 Pa. Code Ch.4 App. C). Front matter pp.1-5 (title, TOC, introduction, chronological periods per grade band). p.6 overview table of the four standard statements A-D (Political and Cultural Contributions; Primary Documents, Artifacts, Historical Places; Continuity and Change; Conflict and Cooperation) with descriptors. Four categories: 8.1 Historical Analysis and Skills Development (A Chronological Thinking, B Historical Comprehension, C Historical Interpretation, D Historical Research), 8.2 Pennsylvania History, 8.3 United States History, 8.4 World History (each A-D). Each category is a table: header row 8.x.3 GRADE 3 / 8.x.6 GRADE 6 / 8.x.9 GRADE 9 / 8.x.12 GRADE 12 (columns C1-C4), a stem row, then rows with lettered statements plus bulleted descriptors and e.g. lists in the same cell (continuation tables lack headers; C1=Gr3, C2=Gr6, C3=Gr9, C4=Gr12). Loose x= text fragments on each page duplicate (mostly) the Grade 3 column. Rows: Gr3 -> K-3, Gr6 -> 4-6, Gr9 -> 7-9, Gr12 -> 10-12. Glossary pp.17-18 (backup).",
